The grammar
description: five constructs, atomic tokens, soft breaks
- >
  Five constructs, and no others. Everything else passes through verbatim.
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Syntax
    - Meaning
      width: 2
  - ['`**bold**`, `__bold__`', strong]
  - ['`*italic*`, `_italic_`', emphasis]
  - ['`~~strike~~`', 'struck through']
  - ['`` `code` ``', 'code span - **atomic**']
  - ['`$$...$$`', 'math, typeset with KaTeX - **atomic**, may span lines']
  - ['`[label](target)`', 'a link - *points at* the target, a yamlover expression']
- >
  **Atomic** means the contents are never re-interpreted as markup: a `*` inside `` `code` `` or
  `$$...$$` is a literal asterisk, not emphasis. Bold is matched before italic, so `**x**` is one
  strong run rather than two emphases. Emphasis **may wrap an atomic token** - `` **`code`** `` is
  a bold code span, `*a `b` c*` an italic run with a code span inside - while a marker *inside*
  the token still can never open or close emphasis. A **link** is an emphasis **boundary**: a
  marker pair spanning one stays literal text; a link styles its own label (`[*a*](b)`).
- >
  An **intra-word `_` is a literal character**, never an emphasis marker - Markdown's rule, kept
  for the same reason: technical prose is full of `snake_case_ids`, and an unbackticked
  `unquoted_scalar_appending` must not italicize its middle. Only a `_` at a word boundary opens
  or closes emphasis (`__` likewise). `*` keeps intra-word emphasis - identifiers don't use it.
- >
  There is **no embed syntax** - marklower delegates structure to yamlover, and embedding *is*
  structure: a chapter body element (see [embeds](*::documents:marklower:embeds)). A `*` before a
  link's bracket is plain text: `*[a](b)*` is a literal asterisk pair around a link (a link is an
  emphasis boundary - italicize the label instead), a bare `*[a](b)` a literal asterisk followed
  by a link. The `*` that matters lives INSIDE the parens, as the target's
  pointer sigil ([link targets](*::documents:marklower:link-targets)).
- >
  Marklower is **not a Markdown subset**, and does not try to be. `![](...)` is not image syntax
  here, and a link target is a yamlover pointer expression, which Markdown has no word for.
- Line breaks
  - >
    A **single newline is a soft break**: the hard-wrapped lines of a block scalar are a *source*
    courtesy, so they rejoin into one flowing run and the rendered prose wraps at the reader's
    chosen width instead of the authored column - Markdown's rule, kept for the same reason. The
    join crosses an inline token (`text\n$$x$$` is one sentence), and emphasis may span it. A
    **blank line stays**: it renders as the vertical gap the author drew.
